Feature: Populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist Table with SQL Logic

  Background:
    Given the source tables are available in the purgo_playground schema
    And the following data is present in the itemledgerentrieswopd table:
      | item_no_ | location_code | posting_date | Expiration_Date | serial_no_ | lot_no_ | other_columns |
      | ITEM001  | LOC001         | 20230401     | 20231231         | SN001      | LOT001  | ...           |
    And the following data is present in the sap_master_data table:
      | Item_No_ | no_ | other_columns |
      | ITEM001  | NO001 | ...           |
    And the following data is present in the item_qty_on_hand table:
      | Item_No_ | location_code | qty_on_hand | other_columns |
      | ITEM001  | LOC001         | 100.0       | ...           |
    And the following data is present in the reservation_entry table:
      | Item_No_ | location_code | reservation_status | source_type | quantity_base | other_columns |
      | ITEM001  | LOC001         | 0                  | 37          | -50.0         | ...           |
    And the following data is present in the Itemwopd table:
      | no_   | Standard_Cost | other_columns |
      | NO001 | 10.5           | ...           |

  Scenario Outline: Successfully populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist with valid data
    When the SQL logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist is executed
    Then a new record should be created in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist with the following values:
      | co_key                      | g_account | g_assignment_type | g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd | g_company_cd | g_company_currency_cd | g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd | g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd | g_item_nbr | g_location_cd | g_location_status_cd | g_lot_effective_dt_yyyymmdd | g_lot_nbr | g_lot_status_cd | g_plant_cd | g_qty_allocated | g_qty_available | g_qty_financial_nettable | g_qty_in_transit | g_qty_mrp_nettable | g_qty_on_hand | g_qty_shippable | g_source_system_cd | g_unit_cost_company_currency | plant_key         | plant_location_key           | prod_key         | prod_plant_key     | prod_plant_location_key             | prod_plant_lot_key           | prod_plant_lot_location_key                 |
      | <co_key>                    | <g_account> | <g_assignment_type> | <g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd> | <g_company_cd> | <g_company_currency_cd> | <g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd> | <g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd> | <g_item_nbr> | <g_location_cd> | <g_location_status_cd> | <g_lot_effective_dt_yyyymmdd> | <g_lot_nbr> | <g_lot_status_cd> | <g_plant_cd> | <g_qty_allocated> | <g_qty_available> | <g_qty_financial_nettable> | <g_qty_in_transit> | <g_qty_mrp_nettable> | <g_qty_on_hand> | <g_qty_shippable> | <g_source_system_cd> | <g_unit_cost_company_currency> | <plant_key>       | <plant_location_key>         | <prod_key>       | <prod_plant_key>   | <prod_plant_location_key>           | <prod_plant_lot_key>         | <prod_plant_lot_location_key>                   |
    Examples:
      | co_key   | g_account | g_assignment_type | g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd | g_company_cd | g_company_currency_cd | g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd | g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd | g_item_nbr | g_location_cd | g_location_status_cd | g_lot_effective_dt_yyyymmdd | g_lot_nbr | g_lot_status_cd | g_plant_cd | g_qty_allocated | g_qty_available | g_qty_financial_nettable | g_qty_in_transit | g_qty_mrp_nettable | g_qty_on_hand | g_qty_shippable | g_source_system_cd | g_unit_cost_company_currency | plant_key        | plant_location_key          | prod_key        | prod_plant_key    | prod_plant_location_key             | prod_plant_lot_key          | prod_plant_lot_location_key                    |
      | nav_ger1050 | ACCOUNT   | Account            | 20230401               | 1050         | EUR                   | 20231231           | 99991231               | ITEM001   | LOC001         | none                | 19000101                   | LOT001   | none            | CAGER      | -50.0           | 100.0            | 100.0                     | NULL             | 100.0                | 100.0         | 100.0           | nav_ger           | 10.5                          | nav_gerCAGER   | nav_gerCAGERLOC001           | nav_gerITEM001  | nav_gerITEM001CAGER | nav_gerITEM001CAGERLOC001           | nav_gerITEM001CAGERLOT001    | nav_gerITEM001CAGERLOT001LOC001              |

  Scenario Outline: Fail to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist due to invalid g_company_currency_cd
    Given the source table item_qty_on_hand contains a record with invalid g_company_currency_cd
      | Item_No_ | location_code | qty_on_hand | other_columns |
      | ITEM002  | LOC002         | 200.0       | ...           |
    When the SQL logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist is executed
    Then the record should not be created in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    And an error message "Invalid g_company_currency_cd: <invalid_currency>" should be logged
    Examples:
      | invalid_currency |
      | USDX             |
      | 123              |

  Scenario Outline: Populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist with default values when fields are missing
    Given the source tables contain records with missing fields
      | item_no_ | location_code | posting_date | Expiration_Date | serial_no_ | lot_no_ | other_columns |
      | ITEM003  | LOC003         | 20230501     | 20240101         |           |         | ...           |
    When the SQL logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist is executed
    Then a new record should be created in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist with default values:
      | g_assignment_type | g_company_cd | g_company_currency_cd | g_location_status_cd | g_lot_status_cd | g_plant_cd | g_qty_allocated | g_qty_available | g_qty_financial_nettable | g_source_system_cd |
      | Account            | 1050         | EUR                   | none                 | none            | CAGER      | <g_qty_allocated> | <g_qty_available> | <g_qty_financial_nettable> | nav_ger           |
    And the following fields should be hardcoded:
      | g_assignment_type | g_company_cd | g_company_currency_cd | g_location_status_cd | g_lot_status_cd | g_plant_cd | g_source_system_cd |
      | Account            | 1050         | EUR                   | none                 | none            | CAGER      | nav_ger           |

  Scenario Outline: Validate date formats in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Given the source tables contain records with dates in incorrect format
      | item_no_ | location_code | posting_date | Expiration_Date | other_columns |
      | ITEM004  | LOC004         | 2023-13-01    | 2024-02-30         | ...           |
    When the SQL logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist is executed
    Then the record should not be created in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    And an error message "Invalid date format for posting_date or Expiration_Date" should be logged
    Examples:
      | posting_date | Expiration_Date |
      | 2023-13-01    | 2024-02-30         |
      | 2023/04/01    | 9999-99-99         |

  Scenario Outline: Handle null values in g_qty_in_transit
    Given the source tables contain a record with null g_qty_in_transit
      | item_no_ | location_code | qty_in_transit | other_columns |
      | ITEM005  | LOC005         | NULL            | ...           |
    When the SQL logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist is executed
    Then the g_qty_in_transit field in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist should be set to NULL

  Scenario Outline: Ensure concatenated keys are correctly formed
    When the SQL logic for f_invntry_bal_dly_hist is executed with the following source data:
      | source_system_cd | g_company_cd | g_plant_cd | g_location_cd | g_item_nbr | g_lot_nbr |
      | nav_ger          | 1050         | CAGER      | LOC006         | ITEM006    | LOT006    |
    Then the concatenated fields should be:
      | plant_key                     | plant_location_key                             | prod_key                   | prod_plant_key             | prod_plant_location_key                   | prod_plant_lot_key                 | prod_plant_lot_location_key                         |
      | nav_gerCAGER                  | nav_gerCAGERLOC006                             | nav_gerITEM006             | nav_gerITEM006CAGER        | nav_gerITEM006CAGERLOC006                | nav_gerITEM006CAGERLOT006          | nav_gerITEM006CAGERLOT006LOC006                    |
